note In the Source view, click a line to select it and shift-click another to extend the selection from the first; the selected lines are highlighted. The reader needs it to say which lines a hand-built step pins, since 'add step' adds the selected lines. A ctrl-, alt- or double-click is a definition gesture, not a selection. The selection is what the Source view's 'add step' adds and what back and forward remember.

